1 Install
*********

Using use-package with a local directory

     (use-package bookmark-gt
       :straight nil
       :load-path "~/.emacs.d/modules/bookmark-gt"
       :bind (("C-x r m" . bookmark-gt-set)         ; supersede built-in bookmark-set
              ("C-x r l" . bookmark-gt-list)        ; supersede bookmark-bmenu-list
              ("C-x r b" . bookmark-gt-jump)        ; fuzzy jump reader
              ("C-x r u" . bookmark-gt-set-url))    ; new: bookmark a URL
       :config
       (bookmark-gt-mode 1))

   Requires Emacs 30.1+.  Soft-deps (loaded when present, package works
without them):

   • ‘marginalia’ — bookmark completion annotator (tags · type · path).
   • ‘consult’ — jump reader UI (falls back to plain ‘completing-read’).
   • ‘orderless’ — enables the ‘,@type’ / ‘;tag’ narrowing particles.
   • ‘browser-gt’ — required only for the browser-tabs feature.  See
     below

   The bindings above rebind the standard ‘C-x r m’, ‘C-x r l’, and ‘C-x
r b’ to the bookmark-gt equivalents.  In particular: prefer
‘bookmark-gt-jump’ over the built-in ‘bookmark-jump’ — the bookmark-gt
reader adds type / tag narrowing, marginalia annotations, MRU-first
sort, and an active-tag filter chip directly in the prompt.
Non-interactive callers should use ‘bookmark-gt-jump’ (or its
‘-other-window’ / ‘-tagged’ variants) so those features are always
available.

