3.2 Jump to a bookmark: ‘bookmark-gt-jump’
==========================================

Recommended replacement for the built-in ‘bookmark-jump’.  The same
command binds naturally to ‘C-x r b’ (see Install) and is the entry
point every other bookmark-gt UI (list buffer, view bookmarks, external
commands) routes through.  Interactive uses, key bindings, and Lisp
callers that need type / tag narrowing, MRU sort, or the mid-read tag
filter should call this instead of ‘bookmark-jump’.

   Uses ‘consult--read’ when consult is loaded, falls back to
‘completing-read’ otherwise.  Both accept two narrowing particles when
orderless is loaded:

   • ‘,@TYPE’ — narrow to bookmarks of TYPE (‘url’, ‘eww’, ‘file’,
     ‘dired’, ‘info’, ‘org’, ‘pdf’, ‘browser-tab’, ‘magit’, ‘help’,
     ‘image’, ‘epub’, or any registered/derived type).
   • ‘;TAG’ — narrow to bookmarks carrying TAG.

   Mid-read tag filter:

   • ‘M-t’ — add a tag filter and restart the read.  Active filters are
     shown as labels in the prompt.
   • ‘M-d’ — pop the most recent tag filter.
   • ‘M-D’ — clear every active tag filter.

