9.1 Selected customization
==========================

Variable                               Default                               What it does
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘bookmark-gt-list-name-width’          ‘32’                                  Character width of the Name column in ‘*Bookmarks-gt List*’.  Longer names are truncated with an ellipsis.
‘bookmark-gt-list-type-width’          ‘12’                                  Character width of the Type column.
‘bookmark-gt-list-tags-width’          ‘24’                                  Character width of the Tags column.
‘bookmark-gt-list-buffer-name’         ‘"*Bookmarks-gt List*"’               Name of the buffer opened by ‘M-x bookmark-gt-list’.
‘bookmark-gt-list-selection-mark’      ‘?*’                                  Character shown in the mark column for rows marked with ‘m’ (a bulk action target).
‘bookmark-gt-list-deletion-mark’       ‘?D’                                  Character shown in the mark column for rows flagged with ‘d’; ‘x’ deletes every row bearing this mark.
‘bookmark-gt-list-default-show-temp’   ‘t’                                   Whether new list buffers show temporary bookmarks by default; toggle per-buffer with ‘H’ (‘bookmark-gt-list-show-temp’).
—                                      —                                     (View bookmarks: no defcustom; save via ‘M-x bookmark-gt-set’ inside the list buffer.)
‘bookmark-gt-jump-name-max-width’      ‘58’                                  Width at which the jump reader truncates bookmark names, so a long name does not push the annotation columns off the window.  Avoid multiples of 10: marginalia rounds its alignment column up to a multiple of 10, so such a value leaves the widest rows no room for the aligning space.
‘bookmark-gt-jump-default-sort’        ‘'mru’                                Sort order used by ‘bookmark-gt-jump’ when no ‘:sort-by’ is given.  Values: ‘'mru’ (most recently used), ‘'visits’, ‘nil’ (pool order).
‘bookmark-gt-dired-virtual-max-size’   ‘524288’                              Maximum bytes of a virtual-dired buffer to inline in a Dired bookmark.  Exceeding this on ‘bookmark-gt-set’ signals ‘user-error’.
‘bookmark-gt-auto-update-interval’     ‘60’                                  Seconds of idle time between ticks of ‘bookmark-gt-auto-update-mode’; each tick refreshes bookmarks carrying ‘auto-update’.
‘bookmark-gt-track-renames’            ‘t’                                   When non-nil, ‘rename-file’ rewrites any bookmark whose ‘filename’ matched the source path to the destination.
‘bookmark-gt-default-tags’             ‘nil’                                 Under ‘bookmark-gt-default-tags-mode’, seeds the tag reader.  Value can be a string, a list of strings, or a function of the record; see the mode's section.
‘bookmark-gt-prompt-for-tags-flag’     ‘t’                                   Whether the tag reader prompts on ‘bookmark-gt-set’.  Off suppresses the prompt globally; batch callers can let-bind ‘nil’.
‘bookmark-gt-same-name-overwrite’      ‘t’                                   *Full collision only* (same name AND handler AND filename): replace the existing record in place rather than appending ‘<N>’.  Has no effect when the filenames differ; see Same-name policy.
‘bookmark-gt-allow-duplicate-names’    ‘t’                                   *Partial collision only* (same name, different filename or handler): store the literal name, letting two records share it.  Off appends ‘<N>’ instead; see Same-name policy.
‘bookmark-gt-highlight-enable’         ‘t’                                   Per-bookmark line overlays in file-visiting buffers.  Off suppresses the overlays even while ‘bookmark-gt-mode’ is on.
‘bookmark-gt-auto-temp-names’          ‘("\\`org-capture-last-stored\\'")’   Names (regexps) auto-marked temporary on 'bookmark-store' — third-party transient bookmarks that should not persist.
‘bookmark-gt-file-type-handlers’       ‘nil’                                 Alist mapping filename regexp to a handler function; when a file bookmark's ‘filename’ matches, the function is called with the record instead of the built-in ‘find-file’ path.
‘bookmark-gt-browser-tabs-browsers’    ‘nil’                                 List of browser-gt browser client names to query for tabs (e.g.  ‘'("chrome" "firefox")’), or ‘nil’ to query every browser browser-gt is connected to.
‘bookmark-gt-browser-tabs-filter’      ‘nil’                                 Filter applied to each fetched tab before it is stored.  ‘nil’ = accept every tab; a regexp = keep tabs whose URL matches; a function = called with the tab plist, kept when it returns non-nil.


